{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfTgPHxLo26FFU4Upv3ku","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I can now provide a complete picture:\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Controllers throw specific exception types: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409)\n2. Exceptions are caught by `GlobalExceptionHandler` which wraps them in `ApiError` with an `ErrorCode`\n3. Repository methods: `save()`, `findById()`, `existsById()`\n4. Test pattern: MockMvc with MockMvcRequestBuilders and jsonPath assertions\n5. Error responses are validated in tests to check both status code and error code\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - must add new error code for cancelled shipment rejection\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - must add POST confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - must add tests for all 4 cases (CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent CONFIRMED, CANCELLED rejection, 404)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. The error code naming needs to follow existing conventions\n2. Idempotency logic must be correct\n3. Must not break existing tests\n4. Status code 200 OK vs 201 Created for the confirm response\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone - the ticket is clear about requirements. I need to add an error code for the CANCELLED rejection case.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` error code to the ErrorCode enum after `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a `confirm()` method:\n   - Maps to `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Finds the shipment or throws `ResourceNotFoundException`\n   - If already CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If CREATED, updates to CONFIRMED, saves, and returns it\n   - If CANCELLED, throws `ConflictException` with the new error code\n   - Returns `ResponseEntity.ok()` with the shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add 4 new test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and returns 200 OK`\n   - `confirm is idempotent for an already confirmed shipment`\n   - `rejects confirmation of a cancelled shipment with 409`\n   - `rejects confirmation of a non-existent shipment with 404`\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using `200 OK` vs `201 Created`: The ticket doesn't specify, but since this is transitioning an existing resource (not creating), `200 OK` is more standard than `201 Created`. The create endpoint uses `201 Created`.\n- Adding error handling in a service layer: The codebase keeps it simple with direct controller logic for CRUD, so I'll keep it in the controller.\n- Using a request body: The ticket shows path parameter only, no body needed.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nCase 1 - CREATED shipment:\n- Request: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n- Read: find shipment by ID from repository\n- Check: status == CREATED\n- Write: save with status = CONFIRMED\n- Return: 200 OK with updated shipment\n\nCase 2 - Already CONFIRMED (retry):\n- Request: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n- Read: find shipment by ID\n- Check: status == CONFIRMED\n- Write: no change needed\n- Return: 200 OK with unchanged shipment\n\nCase 3 - CANCELLED shipment:\n- Request: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n- Read: find shipment by ID\n- Check: status == CANCELLED\n- Throw: `ConflictException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM, message)`\n- Return: 409 Conflict via GlobalExceptionHandler\n\nCase 4 - Non-existent shipment:\n- Request: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n- Read: find shipment by ID returns null\n- Throw: `ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)`\n- Return: 404 Not Found via GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Create shipment, confirm it, verify status changed to CONFIRMED and returns 200\n- Test 2: Confirm same shipment again, verify no change and returns 200 (idempotency)\n- Test 3: Directly insert a CANCELLED shipment into repository, try to confirm, verify 409 with error code\n- Test 4: Try to confirm non-existent shipment, verify 404 with error code\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2314,"cache_read_input_tokens":21045,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2314},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"979f62ad-0872-4b34-a56d-0f4059018d2a","uuid":"4cc169a9-9a38-4d09-9c4c-665ffab1747f","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:07:38.523Z","request_id":"req_011CfTgPHcWwaoPqnSPP2eb6"}
